# Summon Warhorse for Alliance Paladins: The Tome of Nobility (1661) from
# Duthorian Rall in Stormwind's Cathedral of Light teaches it (spell 13820,
# learning Summon Warhorse 13819). Two breadcrumbs send Ironforge paladins to
# him: The Tome of Nobility 4485 from Tiza Battleforge and 4486 from Brandur
# Ironhammer (either race may take them; one closes the other).
# Sources: Forever client 1.60.1.70450 tables (Mount: Summon
# Warhorse, spell 13819, is still a Forever mount; SpellName); Forever's quest
# data for the givers (4485's giver is Tiza on Forever's quest page, a
# correction in forever-db/corrections/quests.json) and the Forever server
# tables (TDB) for the order: 1661 has no prerequisite and teaches the
# spell, 4485 and 4486 teach nothing and form their own exclusive group;
# Warcraft Wiki ("The Tome of Nobility (Ironforge)") puts 1661 after them.
# quests.json also lists 1661 as closed by 4485/4486 (Questie); the TDB and
# the wiki do not, and without 1661 the breadcrumbs would teach nothing, so
# the guide takes 1661 after either. Lint warns that 1661 is not offered once
# 4485 or 4486 is taken: that is the Questie exclusion; the correction in
# forever-db/corrections/quests.json (1661, 4485, 4486) removes it with the
# next data build.
# Riding: Summon Warhorse comes with the riding it needs. In Forever's client
# spell data (1.60.1.70450) the spell that teaches it (13820) teaches Apprentice
# Riding (33388) too, as in Classic, and so does the Forsaken version's
# (1279400); the riding trainers' 90-100 gold Apprentice Riding is not needed.
# A Forever class-quest database lists Apprentice Riding as a reward of The
# Tome of Nobility as well. The client's MountCapability for its mount type asks
# for Riding 0 (60% speed), and PlayerCondition 151683 only for the quest (1661).
# Horde paladins: the Forever client has a Forsaken Summon Warhorse (spell
# 1279399, Mount 2923) and a Summon Forsaken Charger (1296534, Mount 3001);
# news reports name their quests "A Trusty Steed" and "Justice and
# Retribution", but Forever's quest data has no quest, giver or step for
# either yet (searched 2026-10-29), so there is no Horde guide.

step The Tome of Nobility (Ironforge)
  only Dwarf
  zone Ironforge
  when available 4485
  tip At 40 Tiza Battleforge, upstairs in the Hall of Mysteries, sends you to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind (Brandur Ironhammer downstairs gives the same errand; take one). Take the Deeprun Tram to Stormwind.
  level 40
  accept 4485                         -- Tiza Battleforge

step Duthorian Rall
  zone Stormwind City
  when onquest 4485
  turnin 4485                         -- Duthorian Rall

step Duthorian Rall
  zone Stormwind City
  when onquest 4486
  turnin 4486                         -- Duthorian Rall

step Summon Warhorse
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Duthorian Rall stands in the Cathedral of Light. At 40 he offers The Tome of Nobility: accept it and hand it straight back to learn Summon Warhorse. Paladins do not buy a horse.
  level 40
  accept 1661                         -- Duthorian Rall
  turnin 1661                         -- Duthorian Rall: Summon Warhorse
